// SNDINFO - the sound catalogue. Each line maps a LOGICAL name (what the
// code asks for, e.g. A_StartSound("sd/weapon/ppsh/fire")) to a LUMP (the
// actual audio data). ZDoom wiki: https://zdoom.org/wiki/SNDINFO
//
// Two kinds of right-hand column:
//   SD...    our own sound, packed in the PK3 as sounds/<LUMP>.ogg from
//            assets/sounds/<set>/ (the build drops the set folder). The
//            weapon ones are the 25 the CEO approved in D74 and SDIZFIR B
//            (D83), mastered and installed by tools/audio/master_weapon_sfx.py
//            (backlog N9; docs/sound/WEAPON-SOUNDS.md section 10); the enemy
//            ones the 57 of D83 and D86, by tools/audio/master_enemy_sfx.py
//            (N9e; docs/sound/ENEMY-SOUNDS.md section 5.12). The comment
//            says the take.
//   DS...    a Freedoom (IWAD) lump, a PLACEHOLDER: nothing is redistributed,
//            the engine resolves the name against the loaded IWAD. The lump
//            that will replace it is in the comment after "->".
// Replacing a placeholder changes only the right-hand column, no ZScript.
//
// $random (ZDoom wiki SNDINFO; the syntax of gzdoom.pk3's own
// "$random grunt/sight { grunt/sight1 grunt/sight2 grunt/sight3 }"):
// where the CEO approved several takes of one sound (D86), the name the code
// asks for is a $random alias and the engine picks one of its members each
// time it plays. The members are ordinary lines, named <alias>/<take>.

// --- Slot 1: ice axe (D40; the sapper's shovel until 2026-10-13) ----------
// The swing was deliberately silent from 2026-10-13 until N9: Freedoom has no
// neutral whoosh (DSSKESWG is the revenant's wind-up) and the chainsaw
// start-up (DSSAWUP) was rejected by the CEO. Ours is played by the first
// frame of SD_IceAxe's Fire state; the wall sound by SD_IceAxePuff's
// AttackSound. The pickup is ours since D94 (N9e): two takes, $random,
// SD_IceAxe's Inventory.PickupSound.
sd/weapon/iceaxe/swing     SDAXSWG     // take C  the pick cutting the air
sd/weapon/iceaxe/hit       SDAXHIT     // take A  steel pick into a body
sd/weapon/iceaxe/wall      SDAXWAL     // take C  pick on stone
$random sd/weapon/iceaxe/pickup { sd/weapon/iceaxe/pickup/1 sd/weapon/iceaxe/pickup/3 }
sd/weapon/iceaxe/pickup/1  SDAXPKP1    // D94 alt1  steel off a stone floor
sd/weapon/iceaxe/pickup/3  SDAXPKP3    // D94 alt3  the haft into the palm

// --- Slot 2: TT-33 Tokarev -----------------------------------------------
// Pickup: ours since D94 (N9e), two takes, SD_Tokarev's Inventory.PickupSound.
$random sd/weapon/tokarev/pickup { sd/weapon/tokarev/pickup/1 sd/weapon/tokarev/pickup/2 }
sd/weapon/tokarev/pickup/1 SDTTPKP1    // D94 alt1  the slide racked to the stop
sd/weapon/tokarev/pickup/2 SDTTPKP2    // D94 alt2  out of the leather holster
sd/weapon/tokarev/fire     SDTTFIR     // take B  dry, high-velocity crack
sd/weapon/tokarev/dry      SDTTDRY     // take A  hammer on an empty chamber
sd/weapon/tokarev/reload   SDTTRLD     // take A  PARKED: no reload state (D47)

// --- Slot 3: IZh-58 double barrel ----------------------------------------
// The pickup keeps Doom's generic one (D94: all three alternatives NO). The
// shot is take B since D83 and the break-open alt3 since D94 (N9e).
sd/weapon/izh/fire         SDIZFIR     // take B  one barrel, deep boom (D83)
sd/weapon/izh/reload       SDIZRLD     // D94 alt3  heavy and slow, the snap at 0.62 s
sd/weapon/izh/dry          SDIZDRY     // take A  the hammerless lock on nothing

// --- Slot 4: PPSh-41 ------------------------------------------------------
sd/weapon/ppsh/fire        SDPPFIR     // take C  one round: crack, jacket, bolt
sd/weapon/ppsh/pickup      SDPPPKP     // take A  stock, jacket, drum, swivel
sd/weapon/ppsh/dry         SDPPDRY     // take A  an empty drum's hollow clack
sd/weapon/ppsh/reload      SDPPRLD     // take A  PARKED: no reload state (D47)

// --- Slot 5: RPG-7 --------------------------------------------------------
sd/weapon/rpg7/fire        SDRPFIR     // take A  launch and sustainer (the grenade's SeeSound)
sd/weapon/rpg7/explode     SDRPEXP     // take A  shaped charge (the grenade's DeathSound)
sd/weapon/rpg7/reload      SDRPRLD     // take A  a PG-7V pushed into the muzzle
sd/weapon/rpg7/pickup      SDRPPKP     // take A  heat guard and tube
sd/weapon/rpg7/dry         SDRPDRY     // take A  the hammer on an empty tube

// --- Slot 6: ROKS-3 flamethrower -----------------------------------------
// The jet is ours since D94 (N9e): three takes, $random. roks3.zs restarts it
// every 3 tics on CHAN_WEAPON, so a held trigger picks a take per restart.
$random sd/weapon/roks3/fire { sd/weapon/roks3/fire/1 sd/weapon/roks3/fire/2 sd/weapon/roks3/fire/3 }
sd/weapon/roks3/fire/1     SDRKFIR1    // D94 alt1  a broad roar, the igniter's hiss on top
sd/weapon/roks3/fire/2     SDRKFIR2    // D94 alt2  a torch: nozzle whistle and spark
sd/weapon/roks3/fire/3     SDRKFIR3    // D94 alt3  a pump pushing fuel in pulses
sd/weapon/roks3/pickup     SDRKPKP     // take A  the tank pack, fuel sloshing
sd/weapon/roks3/dry        SDRKDRY     // take A  igniter snap, last breath of gas
sd/weapon/roks3/reload     SDRKRLD     // take A  PARKED: no reload state (D47)

// --- Slot 7: hand Katyusha ------------------------------------------------
sd/weapon/katyusha/charge  SDHKCHG     // take A  rails cranked up, 20 tics
sd/weapon/katyusha/fire    SDHKFIR     // take A  six rockets off the rails
sd/weapon/katyusha/burst   SDHKEXP     // take A  one rocket detonating (six at once)
sd/weapon/katyusha/reload  SDHKRLD     // take A  rockets onto the rails, 20 tics
sd/weapon/katyusha/pickup  SDHKPKP     // take A  the rail frame lifted
sd/weapon/katyusha/dry     SDHKDRY     // take A  firing switch on empty rails

// === Bestiary (F5) =========================================================
// Logical names sd/mon/<actor>/<event>; 47 sounds, docs/engine/BESTIARY.md 12.
// Since N9e (D83, D86, D91) 37 of them are ours: an SD lump in the
// right-hand column, or a $random alias over our takes (two of them the
// voices D91 approved: the rifleman's sight, the trooper's idle). The other
// ten are VOICES of the rifleman, the trooper and the General still
// waiting for a take (D91): they keep a Freedoom (IWAD) lump, read at run time and never
// redistributed (tests/test_bestiary.py checks each exists), and the
// comment names the lump that will replace it after "->", the one
// docs/sound/ENEMY-SOUNDS.md has a card for. The General's order is
// DSVILSIT, a creature's sight, until SDGENSUM exists.

